# Visual Studio / VS Code local state.
# .vs/ was already committed by accident: it holds the IDE's workspace state,
# including the absolute path of the repo on this machine (D:\Repos\portfolio)
# and a 300 KB content index. Nothing secret, but it is local machine state,
# it does not belong in a public portfolio repo, and it churns on every commit.
# Adding it here stops NEW commits; run once to stop tracking the existing copy:
#     git rm -r --cached .vs
.vs/
.vscode/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# Editors
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Source material that should never ship: raw captures and project files are
# large and are not what the site serves. Export to assets/thumbs/ instead.
*.psd
*.ai
*.aep
*.prproj
*.clip
/raw/
/material/

# Credentials — nothing here today, and nothing should ever land here.
# Web3Forms' access key is public by design and stays in index.html; any
# key that is NOT public (an API secret, a token) must never be committed
# to a static site, because the browser downloads whatever the page contains.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json
